#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureHelp.tsx
msgid "A <0>preset</0> is a button on the fixture that sets several channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". The channels it leaves unticked stay as they are. To make one quickly, set the faders and press the save button next to the presets."
msgstr "A <0>preset</0> is a button on the fixture that sets several channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". The channels it leaves unticked stay as they are. To make one quickly, set the faders and press the save button next to the presets."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A fixture is one device of your rig, e.g. a PAR or a smoke machine. In Setup mode, press <0>Add fixture</0> in the <1>Fixtures</1> view:"
msgstr "A fixture is one device of your rig, e.g. a PAR or a smoke machine. In Setup mode, press <0>Add fixture</0> in the <1>Fixtures</1> view:"

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A fixture's channel can have a <0>Max while locked</0> (in the fixture editor): while the channel lock is on, the channel never goes above it, whichever fader, preset or view sets it. A laser gets 0, a macro channel running the device's own programs e.g. 50. Its faders show a lock and stop at the maximum (at 0 they are greyed out), and a preset that would set it higher is disabled."
msgstr "A fixture's channel can have a <0>Max while locked</0> (in the fixture editor): while the channel lock is on, the channel never goes above it, whichever fader, preset or view sets it. A laser gets 0, a macro channel running the device's own programs e.g. 50. Its faders show a lock and stop at the maximum (at 0 they are greyed out), and a preset that would set it higher is disabled."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "A preset is a button on a fixture that sets several of its channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". To make one, set the fixture's faders and press the save button next to its presets. Edit the fixture to rename a preset or choose which channels it sets: the ones it leaves out stay as they are."
msgstr "A preset is a button on a fixture that sets several of its channels at once, e.g. \"Warm white\". To make one, set the fixture's faders and press the save button next to its presets. Edit the fixture to rename a preset or choose which channels it sets: the ones it leaves out stay as they are."

