#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureHelp.tsx
msgid "The <0>Address</0> column shows where each channel lands. Fixtures sharing addresses get a warning: on purpose, e.g. two PARs moving together, or by mistake."
msgstr "The <0>Address</0> column shows where each channel lands. Fixtures sharing addresses get a warning: on purpose, e.g. two PARs moving together, or by mistake."

#: src/renderer/src/components/fixtures/FixtureHelp.tsx
msgid "The <0>hint</0> is shown below the faders, for what you need while playing, e.g. \"warm up 2 min before smoke\". Use the <1>description</1> for anything else worth knowing about the device: the DMX mode, DIP switch settings, where it hangs, who it belongs to. It stays hidden until you open it on the fixture."
msgstr "The <0>hint</0> is shown below the faders, for what you need while playing, e.g. \"warm up 2 min before smoke\". Use the <1>description</1> for anything else worth knowing about the device: the DMX mode, DIP switch settings, where it hangs, who it belongs to. It stays hidden until you open it on the fixture."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The app always starts in <0>Show mode</0>: the fixtures and their presets can be played, but not changed, and the Channels view is off. Anything else needs <1>Setup mode</1>: in the <2>Settings</2> view, press <3>Unlock Setup mode</3> and type the password. The first time, there is no password yet: the one you type (twice) becomes it. While Setup mode is open, the top bar says so."
msgstr "The app always starts in <0>Show mode</0>: the fixtures and their presets can be played, but not changed, and the Channels view is off. Anything else needs <1>Setup mode</1>: in the <2>Settings</2> view, press <3>Unlock Setup mode</3> and type the password. The first time, there is no password yet: the one you type (twice) becomes it. While Setup mode is open, the top bar says so."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The app remembers the port it was last connected to, also after a Disconnect. On the next start it connects to it by itself, as long as the widget is plugged in before the app starts; otherwise it starts disconnected: plug the widget in, search the serial ports again and press Connect."
msgstr "The app remembers the port it was last connected to, also after a Disconnect. On the next start it connects to it by itself, as long as the widget is plugged in before the app starts; otherwise it starts disconnected: plug the widget in, search the serial ports again and press Connect."

#: src/renderer/src/components/help/UserManual.tsx
msgid "The channel lock is on after every start, independent of the mode. Lift it in the <0>Settings</0> view, e.g. for a show where the laser hangs high enough: in Show mode with the password, in Setup mode with a confirmation. It then stays lifted, also in Show mode and after Lock, until <1>Turn channel lock on</1> or a restart; the top bar shows <2>Channel lock lifted</2> meanwhile. Turned on again, the locked channels drop to their maximum right away."
msgstr "The channel lock is on after every start, independent of the mode. Lift it in the <0>Settings</0> view, e.g. for a show where the laser hangs high enough: in Show mode with the password, in Setup mode with a confirmation. It then stays lifted, also in Show mode and after Lock, until <1>Turn channel lock on</1> or a restart; the top bar shows <2>Channel lock lifted</2> meanwhile. Turned on again, the locked channels drop to their maximum right away."

